---
description: Prefer real CC0 recordings when adding game sound effects
alwaysApply: true
---

# Sound effects

When a sound effect is needed, choose an existing CC0 field recording first. Do not invent a set of versions by synthesis, pitch-shifting, filtering, or reversal for the user to pick.

A recording counts only when the source describes a real capture (a named device, place, or take). Computer-generated, foley-from-a-tone-generator, and AI-generated files are not substitutes.

Confirm the license on the source page is CC0 or public domain before downloading. Keep the author, page, and license next to the file. Give the user a local audition page of the unmodified recordings and wait for a choice. Do not replace the game's current sound first. Trim leading or trailing silence only after the user has chosen a recording.

If no real CC0 recording fits, say so and ask before making a sound.
